      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Swimwear Fabric Technology</h2>
    </div>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Chlorine-resistant fabrics are engineered to withstand the harsh chemical environment of swimming pools without degrading. These fabrics use specially treated polyester fibers that resist chlorine absorption, maintaining color vibrancy and fabric integrity over extended pool use. Standard swimwear fabrics can degrade after 20-30 hours of pool exposure, while chlorine-resistant fabrics maintain performance for 200+ hours. This durability is essential for competitive swimmers, fitness swimmers, and anyone who uses pools regularly. Our chlorine-resistant fabrics are tested to international standards for pool durability.
    </p>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1.5rem;">
      UPF (Ultraviolet Protection Factor) ratings measure fabric's ability to block UV radiation. UPF 50+ is the highest rating, blocking 98% of UV rays. Our swimwear fabrics achieve UPF 50+ through tight weave constructions and UV-absorbing treatments. This protection is permanent, not washing out over time. UPF protection is essential for beach swimwear and outdoor swim activities where sun exposure is significant. Our UPF-rated fabrics are tested to international standards including Australian/New Zealand AS/NZS 4399 and US AATCC 183 standards.
    </p>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1.5rem;">
      Quick-dry fabrics use hydrophobic treatments that cause water to bead and roll off the fabric surface rather than being absorbed. This technology reduces drying time from 30+ minutes for conventional swimwear to 5-10 minutes for quick-dry fabrics. Quick-dry properties enhance comfort, especially for beach-to-street transitions and active water sports. The treatment is durable through multiple wash cycles while maintaining fabric feel and performance. Quick-dry fabrics are particularly valuable for board shorts, swim shorts, and performance swimwear.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

