      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Swimwear Quality Control Standards</h2>
    </div>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Quality control for swimwear begins with fabric testing before cutting. We verify fabric weight, stretch and recovery properties, chlorine resistance, UPF rating, and color fastness. Swimwear fabrics require specialized testing to ensure they meet functional specifications including stretch percentage, recovery rate, and durability in chlorinated water. Any fabric that doesn't meet specifications is rejected and replaced. Our fabric suppliers are OEKO-TEX and GRS certified, providing traceability and assurance that materials meet international standards for quality and safety.
    </p>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1.5rem;">
      During production, we implement inline quality checks at multiple stages specific to swimwear construction. Cutting supervisors verify pattern accuracy and ensure proper grain direction for stretch fabrics. Sewing line leaders monitor stitching quality, seam consistency, and construction standards including elastic application, lining attachment, and seam sealing for water resistance. Our production floor follows ISO 9001 quality management procedures with documented quality checkpoints. Any garment that doesn't meet quality standards during inline inspection is flagged for rework or rejection.
    </p>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1.5rem;">
      Final inspection occurs after all finishing is complete. Our quality control team conducts AQL (Acceptable Quality Limit) inspections checking seam quality, stretch and recovery, print quality, sizing accuracy, and overall finish. We measure a statistically significant sample from each production batch to ensure overall quality meets or exceeds your specifications. Defective garments are separated, documented, and either reworked or replaced. We maintain acceptable defect rates below 2.5%, which is below industry standards. Our commitment to quality ensures your swimwear meets the expectations of quality-conscious consumers.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

